# Studies of Micro-Genetic Learning Brought about by the Comparison and Solving of Isomorphic Arithmetic Problems.

**Authors:** Cauzinille-Marmeche, Evelyne, Julo, Jean

## Abstract
This study focused on the extent to which the comparison of isomorphic problems might enrich subjects' representations and solving strategies. Results with 166 sixth graders solving isomorphic problems show that comprehension increased as problems were processed and that simultaneous presentation of all problems was more favorable than successive presentation of problems. (SLD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ572803

